{
  "actual_completion_date": null,
  "appeal_start_date": "26/08/2026",
  "application_type_full": "Full planning & demolition in a conservation area",
  "decision_conditions": [
    "Reason : 1 - The proposed house by reason of its design and excessive scale & massing, combined with an inappropriate roof form, would result in an overly large form of development which fails to adequately respond to the constrained nature of the site resulting in less than substantial harm to the West Hill Road Conservation Area with no significant public benefit to outweigh this harm failing to accord with policies LP1, LP2 and LP3 of the local plan, Section 72 (1) of the Planning (Listed Buildings and Conservation Areas) Act 1990, Policy HC1 (C) of the London Plan (2021) and paragraphs 212 and 215 of the NPPF (2024).",
    "Reason : 2 - The proposal by reason of its design and layout would result in substandard accommodation for future occupiers in terms of light levels and outlook to basement bedrooms contrary to London Plan (2021) policy D6, Wandsworth Local Plan (2023) policy LP27.",
    "Reason : 3 - Insufficient information has been provided within the submitted arboricultural impact assessment to ensure that no damage will be caused to nearby trees contrary to Local Plan Policy LP56. ",
    "Reason : 4 - Insufficient information has been provided to demonstrate that the development would provide adequate waste provision for future occupants. The proposal is therefore contrary to Local Plan policy LP2 and the Council's adopted 'Refuse, Recycling and Waste (2025)' SPD"
  ],
  "decision": "Refused",
